# xLaDe Architecture

This document explains the architecture of xLaDe.

xLaDe is a simple python based CLI tool for Linux.
It is an ecosystem based tool for Lean 4 proof assistant.

---

## Core idea

xLaDe adds a small layer above Lean 4.

Normally, projects are run on Lean 4 directly for verification.
xLaDe provides a framework and ecosystem so that the Lean 4 (or any) project can record its environment and then later recreate it easily.

In this process, xLaDe does not modify project or Lean 4.
It externally record and saves the project along with its metadata as an experiment.
Then it can run and build the project later when required.

Along with it, xLaDe provides additional ecosystem help such as external tools for projects.
The advantage is that users do not need to add any code or anything in their projects to enable this.
xLaDe automatically wraps all the projects externally without needing any internal change in the project itself. 

